Yah, in California, USA, where I live, most people visualize
an "elf" as being a little child-like man dressed in green,
with pointy ears, living at the north pole and working for
Santa Claus.

The few that have actually read Tolkien envision beautiful
6-7 foot tall fair-skinned men and women with golden hair
and a magical glow or aura around them, very strong and
wise, and often able to perform substantial magic, such as
creating and using magic rings ("...three rings for elven
kings...") and crystal balls (palantiri).  Pointy ears
strictly optional.  (Tolkien never described elf ears,
one way or another, so his readers are free to envision
them as rounded or pointy, as they please.)

The still fewer who have read other elf myths (Moorcock, etc)
may have still other ideas (such as tall albino creatures
with glowing red eyes, perhaps).

